  "geometryBasis": "The named museum basement footprint and entrance, public walkway, 16-step flight and host wing multipolygon locate the podium and stone and glazed building above. The complex’s other blocks are outside the scope.",
  "sectionBasis": "The museum places its entrance on Vera-Brittain-Ufer about 20 metres from the bridge access; the facade consultant documents a roughly 30 m stone-clad, glazed building, with an inclined glass and foil roof for the upper atrium.",
  "limitations": [
    "The exterior includes the museum entrance and the hotel wing that contains it. The exhibits, other DomAquarée blocks, bridge carriageway and aquarium are outside the scope.",
    "The seven storeys and basement are mapped. Minor walls, materials, window bays, roof sections and museum entrance joinery are approximated from written records and mapped controls.",
    "The city’s source terrain sets the lower promenade and terrace. The precise slender retaining edge along the façade needs bounded rendering clearance to show the lower entrance."
